{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1444123-what-are-the-most-useful-purviews","id":1444123,"title":"What are the most useful Purviews?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-15T20:25:23-07:00","id":1444123,"title":"What are the most useful Purviews?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> What are the most useful/generically applicable purviews? Whether as with specific boons or the innate power.<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T03:48:22-07:00","id":1444148,"title":"","content":"All of the general purviews are good! Genuinely, every purview has at least one boon that is worth it.<br /> <br /> For innate powers from the purviews, I think the ones which generate momentum are weak, while the ones that give you scale or let you gain legend are strong, The innates that let you perceive or sense things are also pretty nice, as are ones which grant immunity - being the 'I see dead people' scion or walking through fire are very flavourful.<br /> <br /> The pantheon signature purviews are much more variable: Theoi is over-powered imo with the shapeshifting skills, while Teotl has a very narrow usefulness and Tuatha de Danann is literally a curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26642-notmidas","name":"notMidas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T05:35:50-07:00","id":1444179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notMidas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1444123-what-are-the-most-useful-purviews?p=1444148#post1444148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tuatha de Danann is literally a curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curse and boon. Geasa can grant you the power to uphold them. If I had a geis to not be defeated by anyone of noble birth, the Condition it should give me Enhancements to fight anyone of noble birth (or at least I know is of noble birth.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T07:25:17-07:00","id":1444202,"title":"","content":"That would make sense but it isn't really in the rules as I read them. Just the momentum for any time your geas gives you trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24383-laughinggull","name":"LaughingGull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T07:46:13-07:00","id":1444204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Condition is a long-term status that lingers on a single character, affecting the challenges they face, and is usually represented as a Complication <b>or Enhancement</b> (or some mixture of the two). </div> </div> </div> Emphasis mine<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This Purview binds the Tuatha and their Scions to geasa of their own and lets them lay geasa on others. It can influence the behavior of those under a geis, <b>granting the power to uphold them</b> or tempting Gods or mortals into breaking their geasa. </div> </div> </div> Emphasis mine<br /> <br /> It's entirely within the rules for the Condition gained from a geis to give you enhancements, and it's one of the options presented under the PSP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T09:03:04-07:00","id":1444213,"title":"","content":"I see your point, but it just doesn't seem terribly clear in the description of the geas condition. It would be nice if they just gave another line explicitly saying you should get an enhancent to uphold your Geas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24383-laughinggull","name":"LaughingGull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T10:10:47-07:00","id":1444219,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think it would have been better to be clearer. However, at least there can be an upside to your geis, if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}